{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FrjnJ1PLpTWHcZRf336cnt","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have enough information. Let me compile the detailed findings:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've comprehensively traced the GKR fractional sumcheck implementation in the STARK GPU prover. Here are the key findings:\n\n### 1. **Fractional Sumcheck Implementation** \nLocated at `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/fractional.rs` (line 491: `fractional_sumcheck_gpu`). Per-round flow:\n- **Kernel launch**: `frac_compute_round_and_revert` (round 0) or `frac_compute_round_and_fold` (rounds 1+) — each computes `s'_t(1)` and `s'_t(2)` on GPU\n- **D2H sync**: `reconstruct_s_evals` (line 331) copies 2 EF values back, derives `s'_t(0)` via algebraic identity\n- **CPU work**: Interpolate degree-2 polynomial, compute `s_t(i)` = `eq(ξ_t, i) * s'_t(i)` for i=1,2,3, then `observe_ext` and `sample_ext` transcript (line 334-339)\n- **Challenge feedback**: New challenge `r` fed back to CPU for next round's fold or M-eval\n\n### 2. **Precompute-M Kernel Timing**\n- **`frac_precompute_m_build_raw`** (line 910): Called **once per window** (w=3 variables), not per-round. Builds 4^w=64-element M matrix from tail points\n- **`frac_precompute_m_eval_round_raw`** (line 944): Called **w times per window** (3 times for GKR window). Extracts s'(1), s'(2) from M via contractions\n- **`frac_multifold_raw`** (line 988): Called **once per window** after all w eval rounds. Folds entire buffer by w challenges at once (or w+1 if pending_fold)\n- **When selected**: Enabled by default; chosen when `rem_n >= min_n` (min_n=22 by default, per line 649) and `w` sumcheck rounds remain\n\n### 3. **Kernel Call Ordering Per GKR Round** \nFor GKR round `j` with `round-1` sumcheck rounds:\n1. **Round 0**: `frac_compute_round_and_revert` (fuses tree revert + compute, line 698)\n2. **Rounds 1..**: FoldEval strategy (default for small buffers):\n   - For each inner round: `frac_compute_round_and_fold` (line 419) — fuses fold-by-r_prev + compute in one kernel\n   - After last inner round: `fold_ef_frac_columns` (line 798) — standalone fold\n3. **OR Precompute-M strategy** (when selected, lines 821-1000):\n   - Per window: `frac_precompute_m_build_raw` → w × `frac_precompute_m_eval_round_raw` → `frac_multifold_raw`\n   - Remaining tail rounds: fallback to FoldEval\n\n### 4. **Overall GKR Phase Structure**\nFrom `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs` (line 404):\n1. **Input evaluation** (line 462-473, `log_gkr_input_evals`): Multi-stream GLOBAL/SCATTER modes; already optimized\n2. **Tree build** (line 517-576): Bit-reversal + fused 2-layer kernels + final single layer\n3. **Root observation** (line 579-594): D2H copy, observe/sample from transcript\n4. **Inner GKR rounds** (line 655-1079, loop `for round in 1..total_rounds`): ~20 rounds at APC 300\n   - Each round has 0-22 sumcheck inner loops (total_rounds = log2_strict_usize(leaves) ≈ 21 for APC 300)\n5. **Finalization**: Layer claims construction (line 1057-1078)\n\n### 5. **Reverted GPU-Side Postprocess**\nCommit `b9b0c0d7` (reverted by 94246cad) attempted GPU-side transcript processing via `gkr_postprocess.cu` kernel. The kernel (now deleted) would have:\n- Reconstructed s_evals on GPU (Lagrange interpolation)\n- Observed s_evals in GPU-resident sponge state\n- Sampled challenge r on GPU\n- Updated accumulators (eq_r_acc, prev_s_eval)\n- **Eliminated**: D2H copy, CPU interpolation, CPU transcript observe/sample per round\n\nThis was reverted, leaving all transcript work on CPU, which is the sequential bottleneck.\n\n### 6. **Time Breakdown (527ms LogUp GKR at APC 300)**\nMetrics labels in code (line 576, 1080):\n- `frac_sumcheck.segment_tree` — tree build (bit-reversal + layers 0-n)\n- `frac_sumcheck.gkr_rounds` — inner GKR loop (all ~20-21 rounds with sumcheck inner loops)\n\n**Per-round estimate**: ~20-22