{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0146mB3dATnrLKBQFggWW4DL","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 2026-04-14-2000-matrix-base-ptr-interpolation\n2\t\n3\tReplace the flat per-column pointer array (~106K entries at APC 300) with per-matrix base pointers (~2K entries) in the batched interpolation kernel used during MLE rounds. Currently, each MLE round rebuilds a `Vec<*const EF>` of all column GPU addresses by iterating O(#total_columns) on the CPU (~1.6ms per round), then uploads it H2D (850KB). By passing per-matrix base pointers and widths instead, the kernel computes column addresses internally via `base + col * height`, reducing the CPU-side collection from O(106K) to O(2K) and the H2D from 850KB to ~40KB per round.\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01JNztHmVdjr4DDDU6TwBd1Y","session_id":"ae9b2456-7a6a-41ad-a41d-1e3f4310411a","uuid":"be0a61e7-f5a8-416c-9732-96573fce9b32","timestamp":"2026-04-14T17:44:25.337Z"}
