{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017SkybkE8eENvVRGd7UH5XL","type":"tool_result","content":"autoopt-results/2026-04-14-2000-matrix-base-ptr-interpolation/plan.md:5:[Omitted long matching line]\nautoopt-results/2026-04-14-2000-matrix-base-ptr-interpolation/plan.md:11:**Phase 1 (mod.rs:1590-1724)**: For each Case B trace, collects per-column GPU pointers into a flat `all_columns: Vec<*const EF>`:\nautoopt-results/2026-04-14-2000-matrix-base-ptr-interpolation/plan.md:14:all_columns.extend(\nautoopt-results/2026-04-14-2000-matrix-base-ptr-interpolation/plan.md:22:At APC 300 with ~600 Case B traces and ~106K total columns (early rounds), this loop takes ~1.6ms per round. Total across all rounds (weighted by decreasing Case B count): ~25-30ms.\nautoopt-results/2026-04-14-2000-matrix-base-ptr-interpolation/plan.md:24:**Phase 2 (mod.rs:1727-1765)**: Uploads `all_columns` to GPU (850KB H2D), builds `InterpColDesc` descriptors (one per trace), uploads those, launches `batched_interpolate_columns_kernel`.\nautoopt-results/2026-04-14-2000-matrix-base-ptr-interpolation/plan.md:28:const FpExt *column = all_columns[d.columns_offset + col_local];\nautoopt-results/2026-04-14-2000-matrix-base-ptr-interpolation/plan.md:194:Replace the `all_columns` collection (lines 1608, 1696-1706) and Phase 2 descriptor building (lines 1727-1765) with the new approach:\nautoopt-results/2026-04-14-2000-matrix-base-ptr-interpolation/plan.md:196:**Phase 1**: Remove the `all_columns: Vec<*const EF>` variable and the per-column `extend` call (lines 1608, 1696-1705). Instead, track per-matrix info alongside CaseBMeta:\nautoopt-results/2026-04-14-2000-matrix-base-ptr-interpolation/plan.md:199:// Replace all_columns with per-matrix collection\nautoopt-results/2026-04-14-2000-matrix-base-ptr-interpolation/plan.md:250:**Why**: This replaces O(106K) pointer computations with O(2K) matrix info pushes per round, and 850KB H2D with ~40KB H2D.\nautoopt-results/2026-04-14-2000-matrix-base-ptr-interpolation/plan.md:260:And update `num_columns` to be computed from matrix widths (as shown in Change 5) instead of from `all_columns.len() - col_start`.\nautoopt-results/2026-04-13-1600-batch-round0-descriptor-arrays/report.md:5:Replace per-AIR Round 0 kernel launches (zerocheck constraint eval + logup interaction eval) with batched descriptor-array kernel launches. Currently, each of ~310 AIRs per segment at APC 300 gets 2+ individual kernel launches, buffer allocations, and H2D copies, resulting in ~1500 kernel launches per segment. Nsys profiling showed 76% of Round 0 wall time (294ms) was overhead, not GPU compute.\nautoopt-results/2026-04-13-1100-batch-mle-interpolation/report.md:5:[Omitted long matching line]\nautoopt-results/2026-04-14-1800-batch-mle-per-trace-h2d/plan.md:5:Replace ~5000 per-trace `main_ptrs.to_device()` H2D copies per segment in MLE `sumcheck_polys_batch_eval` with ~24 bulk per-round uploads. This reduces CUDA API overhead from ~25ms per segment to ~1ms per segment, targeting a 40-50ms improvement on MLE Rounds at APC 300 (currently 162ms).\nautoopt-results/2026-04-14-1800-batch-mle-per-trace-h2d/plan.md:19:       ├─ Phase 2: Batched interpolation kernel (mod.rs:1727-1765) — already 1 H2D per round\nautoopt-results/2026-04-14-1800-batch-mle-per-trace-h2d/plan.md:32:- Phase 1 Case A.1 adds another ~623 H2D copies across all rounds (one per trace at its transition round).\nautoopt-results/2026-04-13-1100-batch-mle-interpolation/plan.md:95:    const FpExt *const * all_columns,\nautoopt-results/2026-04-13-1100-batch-mle-interpolation/plan.md:108:        const FpExt *column = all_columns[d.columns_offset + col_local];\nautoopt-results/2026-04-13-1100-batch-mle-interpolation/plan.md:131:    const FpExt *const * all_columns,\nautoopt-results/2026-04-13-1100-batch-mle-interpolation/plan.md:139:        descs, all_columns, s_deg, num_descs\n\n[Showing results with pagination = limit: 20]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01JNztHmVdjr4DDDU6TwBd1Y","session_id":"ae9b2456-7a6a-41ad-a41d-1e3f4310411a","uuid":"f6501412-9a85-47a8-8fc7-790ae1401765","timestamp":"2026-04-14T17:45:14.148Z"}
